course: dictionary
lesson: 8874
title: One word, three meanings: shortly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shortly is a small word with more than one meaning. The clues around it tell you which one the writer means. «We will be landing shortly» is an announcement on a plane, so shortly means soon, in a short time.
explain: Shortly can also mean in a few words. «No,» she said shortly. The word said tells you she spoke, and the short answer tells you she was impatient or rude. Read the whole sentence before you choose.
explain: Shortly before and shortly after are useful phrases. In «Rabbi Hillel, a Jewish teacher who lived shortly before Jesus, taught…», shortly before means a short time earlier. The writer is placing one person just before another in time, not telling you the exact number of years.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Shortly can mean soon, as in «The bus will arrive shortly.»
fact: Shortly can mean a short time before or after, as in «shortly before» and «shortly after».
fact: Shortly can mean in a few words, often rudely, as in «No,» she said shortly.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The bus will arrive shortly.» What does shortly mean here? | Never | Slowly, over a long time | Loudly | *Soon
exercise: Rabbi Hillel «lived shortly before Jesus». What does shortly before mean? | On the same day, every year | *A short time before | At exactly the same time | A long time after
exercise: «No,» she said shortly. What does shortly suggest? | She was singing happily | She was speaking very slowly | *She was short and a bit rude | She was whispering a secret
test: «We will be landing shortly, so please fasten your seatbelts.» What does shortly mean? | Quietly, like a whisper | *Very soon | Very late, after a long wait | In a few words, rudely
test: «Shortly after the rain stopped, the sun came out.» What does shortly after mean? | Shortly after means a long time after the sun came out | *Shortly after means a short time after the rain stopped | Shortly after means before the rain began | Shortly after means in a rude way
exam: Which sentence uses shortly to mean in a few words, often rudely? | Rabbi Hillel lived shortly before Jesus. | The show starts shortly after lunch. | *«Go away,» he said shortly. | The bus will arrive shortly.
